NAME
    c2c.zoo — the zoo maintenance interface for trained fusers

DESCRIPTION
    Trained fuser weights are published per (Sharer, Receiver) pair
    (FR-15) and resolved offline first: the local zoo in
    $C2C_ROOT/zoo (default ~/.cache/c2c/zoo) is consulted before the
    Hugging Face hub. Pair ids are filesystem-safe, lower-cased,
    separated by a double underscore:

        <sharer>__<receiver>            e.g.  qwen2.5-0.5b__qwen3-0.6b

    Layout of one published pair:

        <pair>/manifest.json      id, revision, sha256, config, provenance
        <pair>/weights.pt         torch.save of state_dict (checkpoint)

    Integrity: the SHA-256 digest recorded in the manifest is verified
    on every download; a truncated transfer is a failed transfer and
    raises — never a warning.

    The unified latent space (EX-1, App. A.5.1-A.5.2): M projectors
    into one latent KV space, N fusers on the receiver side; the
    parameter budget grows O(M+N), not O(M*N). Many-to-one fusion is
    the configuration of Table 13 (two Sharers -> 64.60 average
    accuracy on the Receiver alone).

COMMANDS
    c2c zoo list                    describe the zoo, pair by pair
    c2c zoo publish --sharer ID --receiver ID --checkpoint FILE
    c2c zoo get     --sharer ID --receiver ID
    c2c zoo remove  --name PAIR-ID

SEE ALSO
    c2c(1), c2c.config(5), c2c.fuser(5), the hub's docs (the other
    zoo, the animal farm), and the paper's appendix on where the
    weights come from.

